 "showTitle": "The Hard Saying",
 "title": "No.",
 "dates": "Wednesday, February 24 – Sunday, February 28, 2010",
 "logline": "The morning after, a promise kept two flights down; a laptop, a gossip blog and an empty seat; and on Friday, after the Stations, a question asked on the church steps.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "On the levee, Lena: “And till then, nothing. Nothing either one of us would have to explain. Not to them. Not to Mama. Not in a confessional.” — You: “Nothing.” — Lena: “And you don’t kiss me.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "On I-10, you: “Fridays too. Bread and water.” … From the way-back, Lena: “Nobody asked you, Youngstown.”",
   "if": "s2e17_fridays==\"sincerity\""
  },
  {
   "text": "On I-10, you: “Bread and water. That’s a Tuesday in Ohio.”",
   "if": "s2e17_fridays==\"wit\""
  },
  {
   "text": "On the stairs, Lena: “Please don’t talk to me, Jack,” … “Not till you’re free too.” … “We barely held on last time. I’m not standing on another levee with you. Not till Tuesday’s done.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the phone, you: “I’ll call you Wednesday, Ma. I’ll have something to tell you.” — Ma: “Is it good or bad?” — You: “It’s true.” — Ma: “That’s not what I asked.”",
   "if": "s2e18_ma==\"candor\""
  },
  {
   "text": "On her porch, Skye: “I signed every one. Like a kid with an Advent calendar. You let me count.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "From the turnout, you to Lena: “It’s done. It went badly, but it’s done. I’ll find you tomorrow.” … Lena: “I’ll be here. —L.”"
  }
 ],
